    "recommendations": "Ensuring that the single access point and extended driveway remain clear of parked vehicles and obstructions could significantly improve apparatus entry and exit, particularly when multiple units respond simultaneously. Marking or signing the access point at the street frontage may assist responding personnel in quickly identifying the correct entry under low-visibility or nighttime conditions. Maintaining adequate turning and staging space near the main building and detached structure would support simultaneous operations involving both structures. Communicating the limited rear access to local fire and EMS agencies in advance could facilitate pre-incident familiarization and improve operational planning during an emergency."
