    "recommendations": "Reducing brush concentrations immediately surrounding the structure and creating greater separation between shrub masses and the building perimeter could meaningfully improve defensible space and reduce fuel continuity near the improvement. Where heavy brush extends close to the structure, thinning or removing combustible vegetation within the immediate structure zone would reduce direct fuel exposure and may support suppression operations. Managing vegetation along the single access route, including trimming encroaching brush from the roadway edges and maintaining adequate vertical clearance, would support firefighter access and improve evacuation corridor reliability. Given the single point of ingress and egress, keeping this route passable and clearly defined is a priority. Reducing connected brush across the open terrain surrounding the structure, where feasible within the property boundary, could further interrupt fuel continuity and create additional buffer between approaching fire and the improvement, supporting long-term wildfire resilience."
